MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_001: Another spoonful should do it. Yes, that's it. Perfect.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_002: Is that you, Buccar? Why, I had no idea you\ncould cook!
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_003: Hm. I know a bit about the culinary arts. I can make\ntea cakes, and I brew a decent pot of tea too.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_004: Heeheehee. And here I thought you were just some\nboorish warrior. How very unexpected of you.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_005: This is terribly entertaining. Go on, brew a pot of tea\nfor me too, would you?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_006: I'm sorry, but I cannot do that.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_007: What? How dare you refuse my request!
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_008: I cultivated this skill so that I could take care of\nLady Leda while we were in hiding.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_009: Though Father Mahdel assigned a servant to us, I did\nnot think it wise to rely on someone else's service.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_010: So, I have no intention of offering this skill of mine to\nanyone other than Lady Leda.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_011: I will make no exceptions, even for a young woman\nof noble birth.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_012: I see. You are rather narrow-minded for such a\nrespected champion of House Cohendia, aren't you?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_013: Or is it that you lack confidence in your culinary\nskills and don't dare let me put them to the test?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_014: Olympia, are you questioning my competency in\nmatters of the kitchen?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_015: You wanted tea, did you? If you have any other\nrequests, make them now.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_016: Ah, well, if you insist. Might I trouble you for\nsome tea cakes as well? I am a bit peckish.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_017: Fine. But prepare your taste buds!
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_018: Hehehe! That was delicious. And it was terribly kind\nof you to take my request after all.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_019: Oh! How could I let myself be so easily\nmanipulated?!
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_020: They could've been sweeter, and honestly, they were\nquite hard. But the flavor reminded me of something.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_021: I used a recipe I learned a long time ago. You've\nprobably eaten something like them before.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_022: Hmm... You may be right.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_023: Anyway, I prefer my tea cakes sweeter and softer,\nbut yours were not so bad.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_024: Yes, I approve. And I would be more than happy to\nlet you make them for me again sometime.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_C_025: Bah! No! Never again!
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_001: What is that noise? It's coming from somewhere\naround here. If a thief has broken in...
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_002: Oh, Buccar. I'm sorry. Did I wake you?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_003: Ah, it's you. What are you doing wandering around\nhere in the middle of the night?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_004: Do forgive me. I simply could not sleep no matter\nhow hard I tried. I thought a walk might help.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_005: Hm. Are you in some...distress?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_006: No. But my head has been awash in memories that\nI'm quite unable to free myself from.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_007: And you, Buccar, are at least in part to blame.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_008: Me? What do you mean?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_009: I kept thinking about the tea cakes you made for me.\nAnd I finally remembered what they reminded me of.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_010: There was a servant who cared for me when I lived\nat home. He used to make something very similar.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_011: I have not been in touch with him for some time.\nNow...I can't help but wonder how he's doing.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_012: If it worries you, just write him a letter.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_013: Oh, I cannot. You see...I am a runaway.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_014: I left home—left our mansion—after arguing with the\nhead of my house. I packed my bags without a word.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_015: I didn't even say goodbye to my servant. Surely he\nwould never respond to an ungrateful wretch like me.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_016: You're jumping to conclusions. How about a cup of\ntea to clear your mind?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_017: Thank you. You really do brew a delicious cup of tea.\nIt is very relaxing.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_018: The best remedy for a sleepless night is a sip of\nsomething warm. It calms the mind every time.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_019: He often soothed me in the same way.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_020: And still I repaid his kindness with ingratitude.\nHe must be so angry with me.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_021: Yes, he may be angry at your selfish behavior.\nAnd you may be in for a scolding.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_022: But it's your responsibility to accept his reprimand.\nOr so I believe.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_023: Angry or not, I'm sure he's very worried about you.\nSend him a proper letter, and see if you can meet.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_024: Thank you, Buccar. It's almost as if he himself is\ntelling me what he wants me to do.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_025: You two are about the same age, so perhaps\nthat's why.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_026: Is that right? I suddenly feel a kinship with\nthis fellow.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_027: I will pen him a letter, as you suggested. Though,\nmight I borrow some writing implements?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_028: Mm-hm. And shall I prepare some tea cakes for\nyou as well? Perhaps they'll serve as inspiration.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_029: And here I thought you had vowed never to bake\nfor me again.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_B_030: This is a special case.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_001: Greetings, Olympia. What has put you in such a\ngood mood?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_002: It's the letter I've been waiting for! It just arrived!\nI'm on my way to read it in my room right now.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_003: Ah, it must be from the servant we spoke about.\nI've never met him, but I feel like I know him.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_004: We work so hard to serve our strong-willed ladies,\ndon't we? I must help Olympia understand that.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_005: I hope this exchange allows them to begin speaking\nto each other once more. Yes, a fresh start.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_006: Perhaps I'll bring her some tea and some tea cakes\nas well.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_007: Olympia, I'm coming in. I thought you might want\nto discuss your letter over a cup of tea.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_008: *sob* Buccar?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_009: You seem unhappy. What did the letter say?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_010: He...he died during a terrible epidemic...not long\nafter I left home.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_011: My father wrote to me on his behalf.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_012: What? Oh no...
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_013: I never got the news—in part, because I left.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_014: But also...my father said he wanted to spare me the\ngrief as long as he could.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_015: He enclosed in the letter...a memento.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_016: You don't mind showing it to me?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_017: I'm certain you could put it to better use than I could.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_018: Hm... This is his tea-cake recipe.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_019: Ah. Look at this... His is a bit different from mine.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_020: The ingredients and quantities he used would have\nmade his cakes much sweeter.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_021: According to the notes, he experimented with the\nrecipe until shortly before he died.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_022: He wrote, "When the young lady returns home,\nI hope she enjoys how sweet my new tea cakes are."
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_023: Ah... I see.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_024: He changed them to try and suit my taste.\nBut he didn't need to do any such thing...
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_025: I loved them when they were hard and not very\nsweet. They were delicious and perfect.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_026: Oh, Olympia...
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_027: You could have stayed home and remained close\nto him...
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_028: But you did not, because that's not what you\nwanted from life, correct?
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_029: No. I never would have blossomed in that house.\nI...I don't regret leaving.
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_030: But just for now...just for a moment...would it be\nalright if I rested my head on your shoulder and...
MID_SE_Buc_Oly_A_031: Yes, let me take his place for a moment...and let the\ntears flow.